      "verification": "Checked by hand on 2026-11-04 against MetaData.docx, the paper and its SI Appendix (read in full: Materials and Methods, Fig. S1, Table S1). Files: the zip's MD5 and size are those Figshare publishes (8ddf1504..., 658,989,513 bytes); its SHA-256 was computed from one full download; each member read is pinned by its own SHA-256. MATLAB versions: lfp.mat 7.3 (HDF5), the others 5.0. Order of the cells: the share of rewarded free-choice trials follows Table S1's Performance column row by row, 78.3% against 78.2% here, and the paper's rule for complex-spike cells gives 648 of 698 units over all cells, the paper's number. Time: 130,079 samples at a median 0.03352 s (29.8 Hz, the SI's 30 Hz), 632.3 to 4973.2 s; the units' spikes lie inside it; lfp.mat is 2 kHz with no gap, from 632.287 s. Trials: 159 of events.mat match beh.mat row by row at shift 0: the start of reward equals beh.mat's last sensor plus one constant, 20 ms median difference, one row (the last of session 1) 44 s off. Two sessions of four blocks in random order, the head clusters at the reward site at the start of reward, and each trial's label names the arms the head ran through. Position scale: not stated; 3.6 pixels per cm from the 300 cm linearized maze of Fig. 3A and the 30 cm from nozzle to trial start. Heading against movement: +4.3 deg mean, 15 deg spread, after converting the stored bearing. LFP: 21.4% of samples at +/-327.67; population rate 1.52 times baseline at ripple-power peaks. Overview figure and animation frames looked at: the path runs the maze's loop, the head sweeps at the reward site, the rate of off-maze samples is low on this set; the Environment panel is squeezed by a legend with one entry per graph edge (a plotting issue, not the data)."
    },
